                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" disabled="@(itemModel is null || macroblockInstances.Count == 0)" @onclick="ExportMultiInstanceItemGbx"
                            title="Embeds the copies into one item: a root prefab with one entry per copy, all referencing the same mesh.">
                        📦 Export multi-instance .Item.Gbx (mesh embedded once)
                    </button>
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-2">
                        The macroblock export references the item by ident (Trackmania resolves it from
                        your inventory), while the multi-instance item embeds the mesh once and repeats
                        only a transform per copy — one file, no external item needed. Each copy keeps its
                        own position and rotation relative to the root; prefab entries cannot carry a
                        scale, so scaled copies are exported at scale 1 with a note in the status line.
                    </p>
                    <p class="small text-muted mt-2">
                        The export reparses its own bytes with the parser used for import and refuses to download
                        a file that cannot be reopened. Trackmania resolves the copies through the item ident, so
                        the item has to exist under that ident in your inventory.
                    </p>
                }

            </div>
            
